  <!-- ============ SECTION 27 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s27"><span class="num">27</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="three-col">
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Abschlussprüfer</div><div class="glossary-def">Statutory auditor — the person or firm engaged to perform the mandatory audit.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Unternehmen von öffentlichem Interesse (PIE)</div><div class="glossary-def">Public-interest entity — capital-market-oriented companies, CRR credit institutions, and insurance undertakings, per §316a.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Bestätigungsvermerk</div><div class="glossary-def">The short, public-facing audit opinion — unqualified, qualified, adverse, or a disclaimer.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Prüfungsbericht</div><div class="glossary-def">The detailed, generally-internal audit report covering significant findings and risks.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">FISG</div><div class="glossary-def">The 2021 Finanzmarktintegritätsstärkungsgesetz, Germany's legislative response to the Wirecard scandal, which reshaped §316a and §323.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Haftungshöchstgrenze</div><div class="glossary-def">Statutory liability cap — the tiered EUR ceiling on an auditor's negligence-based liability under §323(2).</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

